8133501,2024-01-10,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Improper use of your report,Reporting company used your report improperly,"According to the Fair Credit Reporting Act ( FCRA ) 15 USC 1681 section 602 ( a ), it is essential to ensure that consumer reporting agencies carry out their significant responsibilities with fairness, impartiality, and respect for the consumer 's privacy rights. As a consumer, I have the right to safeguard my private information, as supported by 15 USC 6801, which emphasizes the Congress 's policy that financial institutions must actively protect customer privacy and the confidentiality of nonpublic personal information.

A "" furnisher of information to credit agencies, '' classified as a financial institution, falls under this title. 15 USC 1681 section 604 ( a ) ( 2 ) stipulates that a consumer reporting agency may only provide a consumer report in accordance with the written instructions of the respective consumer. I want to make it clear that both the financial institution ( Furnisher of information to credit agencies ) and the consumer reporting agencies, Equifax and XXXX, lack my consent to furnish this information, and they certainly do not possess my written consent. Any form of consent, whether verbal, non-verbal, written, implied, or otherwise, granted to Equifax, XXXX, or the Furnisher of information to credit agencies is hereby revoked. 

