According to 15 U.S. Code 1681s2 ( a ) ( 1 ) ( A ), a person must not furnish information to a consumer reporting agency if they know or have reasonable cause to believe the information is inaccurate. 15 U.S. Code 1681e mandates every consumer reporting agency to maintain reasonable procedures to prevent violations and restrict the furnishing of consumer reports to specific purposes. Equifax and XXXX are failing to uphold reasonable procedures. 

