8146332,2024-01-11,"Money transfer, virtual currency, or money service",Domestic (US) money transfer,Fraud or scam,,"I left Bank of America after 15 years. I had {$1500.00} left in my checking 's account. They mailed me the final amount to my apartment address in XX/XX/XXXX. I have never had mail compromised or stolen at this address. In XX/XX/XXXX, I received a letter from BoA that captured check # XXXX endorsed and cashed by an unknown woman who forged my name and signed her name on the check ( "" XXXX XXXX '' ). I do not know this woman nor did I give her consent to take or cash my check. The capture date was XX/XX/XXXXXXXX  meaning BoA had notice this forgery took place. I immediately contacted BoA. For the remainder of XXXX, I called every other month to check on the status of BoA refunding my money ; every person I spoke to guaranteed they would yet BoA never did. A representative recommended as a last ditch effort to submit a written fraud claim and mail it to their XXXX office. I spent {$13.00} on certified mail. I filled out the form BoA provided, including getting a notary public to notarize my affidavit of events. I submitted the letter in XX/XX/XXXXXXXX  ; BoA received it on XX/XX/XXXX. They said it would take 45 days to decide. I never heard back. On XX/XX/XXXX, I called BoA and was told my fraud claim was denied. They could not provide me a reason why or what additional information they needed to make a different decision. No one would tell me what the appeals process would be. My information was given to the investigator and told he would call me the following day. He never did. I have still not heard from BoA. I'm at a loss. I was robbed. I filed a police report. I spoke to various BoA departments over the last year totaling HOURS, I followed BoA instructions, and still have not been made whole. I am at a loss for what to do next so I am submitting this complaint on XX/XX/XXXX in order for CFPB to investigate or attempt to make things right. Thank yo