My case did go to appeals and I uploaded all my tax documents for the transactions requested. I had one pending claim open which I had already refunded to the customer. That claim was sided with me but I let the refund remain and did not ask to be repaid. When sent that notification I was also sent an email saying that my account was closed permanently because too many customers were unhappy with my business. This does not seem correct or valid considering Paypal sided with me. Other than this claim I had one other claim for {$11.00} which was also refunded to the customer. In all 4 years of my account being open these were the only 2 claims. This is not a pattern or a continued issue. 

